l oral glucose tolerance, abnormal salivary gland morphology, abnormality of body weight\n  Favours second: abnormal abdomen morphology, abnormal blistering of the skin, abnormal gastrointestinal motility, abnormality of the thyroid gland, acanthocytosis\n\nInsulin Resistance / Metabolic Syndrome vs Ectopic ACTH Syndrome (Hypercortisolism):\n  Favours first:  abnormal circulating fatty-acid concentration, abnormal circulating lipid concentration, abnormal oral glucose tolerance, abnormal salivary gland morphology, abnormality of body weight\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n\nGlucagonoma Syndrome (Alpha Cell Tumor) vs Ectopic ACTH Syndrome (Hypercortisolism):\n  Favours first:  abnormal abdomen morphology, abnormal blistering of the skin, abnormal gastrointestinal motility, abnormality of the thyroid gland, acanthocytosis\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n\nRelated to Insulin Resistance / Metabolic Syndrome: diabetes mellitus (disease)\n\nRelated to Glucagonoma Syndrome (Alpha Cell Tumor): pancreatic neuroendocrine tumor\n\nRelated to Ectopic ACTH Syndrome (Hypercortisolism): adrenal gland disease, neoplastic syndrome\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  He also has experienced abdominal pain and diarrhea → nausea and vomiting → Glucagonoma Syndrome (Alpha Cell Tumor)\n  He also has experienced abdominal pain and diarrhea → poor appetite → Glucagonoma Syndrome (Alpha Cell Tumor)\n  He also has experienced abdominal pain and diarrhea → episodic abdominal pain → Glucagonoma Syndrome (Alpha Cell Tumor)"}
